],[23776,20.0,2020,61,79,26]],"links":[["Sanpete County in the Farmland Atlas","/farmland-atlas/utah/sanpete-county"],["ARC or PLC in Sanpete County","/arc-plc/utah/sanpete-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record for Sanpete County runs from 1951 to 2025, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 15 grids January to February came in under 90% of normal in 38 of those 75 years. In 2025 the middle of the grids got 13% of normal in June to July and 49% in May to June. June to July is the driest pair at 2.08 inches normal, and February to March the wettest at 3.97 inches. Grids 22872 and 23172 both had their driest year in 2020 at 44%.</p>"}
